; ============================================================================
; DR FORTRESS AI V13 FIX24
; FIX24 early mobilization / stronger targeted rescue / gate-throttle repair:
; - Feudal GROWTH now guarantees an early cheap defensive field core instead of waiting until minute 21-25.
; - RECOVERY actively refreshes cheap+middle family requests; weakness means mobilize, not military paralysis.
; - Rescue has its own lower executable group minimum: roughly 40 percent normal / 60 percent critical in one coherent group.
; - Rescue stores a concrete allied player ID when an ally is visibly collapsing and focuses the intervention on that player.
; - automatic Rescue starts earlier from TC/villager/military collapse; critical collapse escalates the committed share.
; - legacy "insufficient army" gating cannot suppress Rescue/Peace Pressure and no longer expects a 40-pop field army.
; - ASSAULT and Peace Pressure group sizes are reduced to values that can actually form from realistic Fortress armies.
; - gate construction is pending-aware and receives a 150-second failed-placement lock to eliminate repeated gate command storms.
; - FIX21 Economy Governor, FIX22 single Attack Owner architecture, FIX23 ERR2004 ordering repair and no-cheat policy are retained.
; - elite guarantee is intentionally unchanged; FIX24 repairs the basic military motor first.
; FIX23 HD parser forward-reference hotfix:
; - fixes ERR2004 on df13-defense-state by declaring the goal before its first executable use.
; - adds no gameplay rebalance versus FIX22; ally rescue, single attack owner, peace-pressure, elite guarantee and FIX21 Economy Governor are unchanged.
; - static validation now explicitly rejects every defconst that is first used before its declaration.
; FIX22 unified attack owner / real ally rescue / peace-pressure / elite guarantee:
; - makes the final Fortress layer the sole writer of createarmy, sn-number-attack-groups, sn-percent-attack-soldiers and attack-now.
; - retires inherited Resonance/Fortress attack-state writers instead of merely overriding them later in the rule pass.
; - real ally rescue commits about 40 percent of the existing field army toward enemies near allies for a timed intervention.
; - rescue can override local DEFENSE/RECOVERY while one local defend group is deliberately retained.
; - ally requests plus severe allied TC/villager/military collapse can trigger rescue; the force is released when the rescue window ends.
; - four minutes of calm STABLE/ASSAULT economy arms a pressure window so a healthy Fortress cannot remain passive forever.
; - ASSAULT entry emits one attack pulse; STABLE peace-pressure emits a controlled attack pulse; no legacy attack-now remains active.
; - a compact four-slot elite guarantee rotates Champion / Arbalest / Paladin / Siege Onager without replacing the middle-tier backbone.
; - Economy Governor remains the FIX21 design; only soft ASSAULT reserve thresholds and Feudal GROWTH food bias are gently tuned.
; - no resource creation, no new wall/formations/civ systems, and no new executable vocabulary beyond FIX21 parser-proven tokens.
; FIX21 Fortress Economy 2.0 / economy-governed tier quality:
; - adds a five-state no-cheat Economy Governor: GROWTH, STABLE, DEFENSE, RECOVERY, ASSAULT.
; - economy state, not short military-population fluctuations, now owns df15-tier-posture.
; - GROWTH/DEFENSE/RECOVERY bias cheap+middle; STABLE keeps middle backbone; ASSAULT unlocks controlled elite bias.
; - dynamic gather profiles react to food/wood/gold/stone scarcity without creating resources.
; - retires the inherited large market rule pile and replaces it with a throttled emergency Market stabilizer.
; - land trade is allowed only from a calm STABLE/ASSAULT economy with an allied Market, making Imperial trade a safe long-term gold engine.
; - ASSAULT economy has entry/exit reserve hysteresis so spending one unit does not instantly flap posture.
; - FIX20 wall owner, no-cheat policy, garrison hysteresis, surrender and posture-weighted tier families are retained.
; - parser safety: no new executable fact/action identifier; only parser-proven FIX20 vocabulary plus new goal/timer constants.
; FIX20 posture-weighted short-cycle tier repair:
; - replaces FIX18/19 long linear tier rotors with six-slot posture-weighted pools; middle tiers are the standing backbone.
; - recovery/defense/low-military remaps every slot toward cheap+middle tiers immediately; assault remaps toward middle+elite.
; - an already researched higher-tier slot NEVER advances to a cheap fallback merely because current stock is low; the request waits.
; - Castle-age middle/elite reserve thresholds are lowered for the legitimate no-cheat economy.
; - Mangonel/Onager/Siege Onager and Battering/Capped/Siege Ram use the same posture logic; Onager/Capped Ram are the standing backbone.
; - parser safety: no new executable identifier is introduced; all train/research tokens are inherited from parser-proven FIX19 vocabulary.
; FIX19 parser repair for FIX18 deterministic tier dispatcher:
; - HD 5.8 ERR2004 at FIX18 line 28516: base militia identifier is militiaman, not militia.
; - replaces every new base-tier (can-train militia)/(train militia) occurrence with the parser-proven militiaman identifier.
; - no gameplay rebalance versus FIX18; all no-cheat economy, tier reservation, wall/palisade, build-lock, garrison and surrender changes are retained.
; FIX18 no-cheat stable-fortress / deterministic-tier / construction-state repair:
; - legitimate economy only: inherited resource-creation rules are removed as whole rules, not merely muted actions.
; - economy is deliberately slower and steadier after cheat removal: defensive reserves, balanced gather profiles and less premature attack commitment.
; - deterministic per-family tier reservation makes middle tiers the army backbone while cheap and elite researched models remain represented.
; - researched custom-DAT upgraded models are trained directly from research state; false can-train results cannot force base-tier spam.
; - Fortress is the only wall/gate command issuer; Feudal palisade stages persist and wall retries are separately throttled.
; - key building requests have script-level cooldowns so invalid placement cannot generate command storms.
; - defense uses calm-window hysteresis before releasing sheltered villagers.
; - autonomous surrender requires genuine economic + military + structural collapse under pressure, with extra tolerance in team games.
; - FIX17 stability, early allied-help, defensive production continuity, fortress assault and difficulty-independent wall quality are retained.
; FIX17 production / defense / team / fortress coordination repair:
; - fixes the core FIX15/FIX16 tier bug: a family request no longer selects one exclusive tier.
; - middle tiers are the standing-army backbone (Long Swordsman, Pikeman, Crossbowman, Cavalier, Onager, Capped Ram).
; - cheap legacy tiers remain useful supplements/emergency mass; researched elite tiers are guaranteed a recurring share.
; - Paladin/Halberdier/Champion/Arbalest/Siege Onager can no longer be starved merely because the base tier is cheaper.
; - defensive state explicitly keeps createarmy enabled and refreshes family requests on a safe 10-second cycle.
; - Mangonel/Ram family caps are reduced and their dispatch strongly favors Onager/Capped/Siege tiers once available.
; - Standard is correctly mapped to difficulty==easy; Moderate remains difficulty==moderate.
; - inherited Easy timed attack/forced-retreat windows are retired for Standard; FIX17 uses army-size pacing instead.
; - all difficulty levels now use the same wall footprint/expansion intelligence; difficulty changes combat tempo, not wall quality.
; - Feudal palisade planning is isolated from inherited stone-wall goals; Stone Wall takes over in Castle Age.
; - siege wall targeting alternates breach/exploitation windows so armies do not chew adjacent walls forever after opening a path.
; - team games enable cooperative target sharing much earlier so allies can react to pressure before the late-game timers.
; - Trade Cart production is difficulty-capped and serialized to prevent queue bursts on Moderate/Standard.
; - blocked building placement is abandoned after one failed candidate instead of repeatedly hammering the same spot.
; - early local exploration is extended and captured livestock is returned to the TC; no resource/vision cheats are added.
; - no FIX13-rejected executable identifier is reintroduced; only vocabulary already active in FIX16 is used.
; FIX16 crash-safety / wall planner / Standard-tempo repair:
; - crash replay 2026-08-18 02:43 ends abruptly at 22:28.45 with no resign/postgame while the record stream itself parses cleanly to EOF.
; - all three FIX15 players produced ZERO WALL actions; the only four WALL actions in the replay belong to the human player.
; - removes FIX15's repeated 25-second build-wall calls that bypassed can-build-wall and retires timer 49 from the wall layer.
; - Fortress explicitly enables the inherited wall goals; new wall actions are guarded by can-build-wall or can-afford-complete-wall.
; - Feudal wall geometry escalates through a few one-way stages instead of repeatedly hammering the wall planner.
; - the first/inner defensive line is difficulty-independent; Hardest alone keeps the additional outer/deep fortress rings.
; - Standard/Moderate keeps the same wall capability but forms fewer, larger offensive groups and waits for a larger field army.
; - mixed-tier posture no longer writes the balanced goal unconditionally every rule pass.
; - no new executable identifier is introduced; only FIX10/FIX13-proven facts/actions are used.
; FIX15 situational mixed-tier / wall reliability repair:
; - replay 2026-08-18 01:53 (HD 5.8) contains ZERO WALL actions from FIX14 despite long Feudal/Castle play.
; - Feudal palisade bootstrap now retries a direct parser-safe build-wall command on a cooldown until real wall segments exist.
; - wall state/progression is confirmed by actual wall segment counts; issuing a command alone never marks the fortress as started.
; - Feudal Watch Tower floor on Hardest is four towers (FIX14 replay produced only two per Fortress AI).
; - normal military production no longer saves exclusively for the strongest researched tier.
; - tier posture is situational: cheap mass/rebuild/pressure, balanced middle tiers, and elite power tiers for a funded assault.
; - every normal dispatcher can fall back to a cheaper researched tier when the preferred tier is temporarily unaffordable.
; - family requests still come from civ strategy/threat counters, so tier choice and unit-role choice remain separate decisions.
; - no new executable identifier is introduced; FIX10/FIX13 parser-safe vocabulary is retained.
; FIX14 researched-tier production priority (superseded by FIX15 situational selection):
; - replay 004756 confirmed that upgraded tiers were researched while normal production kept buying legacy tiers.
; - FIX14 gave exclusive priority to the strongest researched tier; FIX15 deliberately replaces that behaviour.
; FIX13 AoE2 HD parser compatibility hotfix:
; - removes all active FIX11-only executable identifiers not present in known-good FIX10.
; - directly fixes ERR2004 on up-idle-unit-count and pre-empts the same class of parser failure.
; FIX12 HD parser hotfix:
; - removed unsupported up-reset-placement (ERR2004 in AoE2 HD runtime).
; - failed farm placement recovery now relies on the existing cooldown/retry path;
;   no replacement command outside the already parsed FIX10/FIX11 vocabulary is introduced.
; FIX11 economy/safety/naval recovery:
; - Farm Manager 2.0 replaces the FIX10 hard 420W gate with a soft 3/4/5-reseed reserve (180/240/300W).
; - critically low food overrides the reseed reserve so farms can be placed before the reserve is restored.
; - blocked farm placements are reset after the cooldown instead of permanently locking farm production.
; - persistent idle-villager signals gently recycle one stone/gold gatherer without direct object-search DUC.
; - wounded early Scout Cavalry uses recent HD threat data and retreats to a safe/healing anchor instead of continuing exploration.
; - Dock construction is serialized with pending-object checks and a retry cooldown to stop dock-order floods.
; - idle naval explorers are periodically reissued water-scout work; enemy water presence releases them back to naval combat logic.
; - recent enemy threats against civilians temporarily contract economic drop/camp radii and retask a small worker sample.
; - FIX10 wall placement/geometry rules are intentionally unchanged.
; FIX10 research/wall/farm/monk repair:
; - military tier unlocks are now systematically researched because the custom DAT keeps all older tiers trainable.
; - normal production prefers the best exact tier that is currently affordable; recovery still deliberately buys cheap legacy tiers.
; - family-level can-train gates no longer block a cheaper exact-tier fallback.
; - Fortress wall placement is explicitly enabled on Tiny/Small/Medium maps; Outpost logic no longer overwrites wall geometry.
; - Feudal palisade continuation targets a meaningful defensive line instead of stopping at 35 percent.
; - farm construction is globally throttled with a wood reserve so repeated farm replacement cannot consume the economy in a burst.
; - monk massing is capped and Illumination/monastery upgrades are encouraged to reduce low-faith retry pressure.
; - the inherited setup warning no longer mistakes 200 gathered gold for non-standard starting resources.
; FIX09 custom-DAT multi-tier production doctrine:
; - designed for empires2_x1_p1(1).dat where researched tiers unlock as separate paid units.
; - old tiers remain trainable after later research and are intentionally used as economic/tactical choices.
; - inherited *-line train actions are routed through exact-tier family request dispatchers.
; - recovery/army-rebuild prefers cheap legacy tiers, balanced economy prefers middle tiers, rich assault prefers top tiers.
; - exact family counting/threat detection still uses *-line where it is useful and safe.
; - Barracks, Archery Range, Stable, Siege Workshop, Dock and Castle unique-unit production are covered.
; - FIX08 formation, defense, retreat, scout, wall and command behavior is preserved.
; FIX08 replay/command repair:
; - custom taunt/command interface is enabled by default (command 125 can still disable it explicitly).
; - strategy command layer is open at startup instead of silently requiring a hidden unlock first.
; - military-collapse recovery rebuilds a mixed defensive army after catastrophic losses.
; - inherited land retreat/advantage checks use target-player instead of an unrelated any-enemy.
; - Dark/early-Feudal reconnaissance ignores incidental enemies while scouting and captured livestock returns to the TC.
; - Feudal palisade remains a compact inner security layer; Castle/Imperial stone-wall distances are unchanged.
; FIX07 parser repair:
; - HD legacy parser compatibility: invalid relational goal tests were replaced with exact-stage OR tests.
; - fixes ERR2011 at former line 28572 and the two equivalent latent errors later in the wall/gate block.
; FIX06 multiplayer replay repair (Mediterranean / 150 pop / Very Hard):
; - Fortress walls are permanent strategic infrastructure; inherited wall deletion is disabled.
; - Castle-age developed walls never downgrade from stone to palisade.
; - base expansion is additive: old rings stay, larger outer stone envelopes are added.
; - local Outposts use an envelope three town-size steps inside the planned local wall.
; - mature fortresses add gates under serious path/resource-walking stress instead of deleting walls.
; - Scout Cavalry is a separate paid tier: max 6 total on Hardest, max 3 on Moderate.
; - Scout -> Light Cavalry -> Hussar and Knight -> Cavalier -> Paladin use exact tier-aware production.
; - common infantry/archer/spear/cavalry/siege/naval upgrades seed the newly researched full-price tier while old models remain.
; FIX05 replay repair: mandatory Feudal wall bootstrap, stronger Castle wall continuation,
; coherent 10+ land combat groups, and siege-gated wall/gate targeting.
; FIX04 communication overhaul:
; - all Fortress chat strings use a new military/fortress-command voice
; - inherited Resonance-style self-identification and banter were removed/reworded
; - tactical meaning, ally requests, command numbers and setup warnings are preserved
; Architecture reset: ResonanceBot 5-1c is the economic / civilian / age-up core.
; Fortress is a defensive, military and siege doctrine layered on top.
;
; IMPORTANT DESIGN RULES
; - Opening civilian tasking is intentionally left to ResonanceBot.
; - Dark -> Feudal -> Castle -> Imperial economy is intentionally ResonanceBot.
; - Fortress never enters a dedicated Castle-saving economy.
; - Castles are opportunistic high-value defensive anchors: build only when the
;   normal economy already makes one affordable and the placement has value.
; - Fortress adds fortification, threat memory, defensive formations, civ-aware
;   production, siege packages, recovery, concentrated counterattacks and
;   population profiles for 125 / 150 / 200.
;
; Original ResonanceBot code below remains attributed to @Resonance22.  V13 is a
; derived experimental AI for Age of Empires II HD, not the original bot.
